  "topic": "Concurrency and Synchronization Primitives using Pthreads",
  "explanation": "Concurrency allows multiple threads of execution within a single process to run seemingly simultaneously, improving performance by overlapping computation.  Synchronization primitives are mechanisms to coordinate these threads, preventing race conditions and ensuring data consistency.  Pthreads (POSIX threads) is a widely used standard for creating and managing threads in Unix-like systems. This is crucial in computer systems architecture for maximizing CPU utilization and handling multiple tasks efficiently.",
